{"commit": "a5745baa172d50679e34b33d6dba3d063eb40cd4", "id": "a5745baa172d50679e34b33d6dba3d063eb40cd4-1", "language": "rust", "reason": "Selected test is not present at the fixed revision: reader::tests::comment_5", "repo": "https://github.com/BurntSushi/rust-csv", "reproduction": {"attempt": "20260924T002633Z-fcf2ace4", "evidence_sha256": {"evidence/a5745baa172d50679e34b33d6dba3d063eb40cd4-1/20260924T002633Z-fcf2ace4/origin.json": "20fb75395452d24e9a2c7b3274e25715bb524a52d3c8fd3ecacca1f0b986c1d5", "evidence/a5745baa172d50679e34b33d6dba3d063eb40cd4-1/20260924T002633Z-fcf2ace4/proposal.json": "bdbd708c7625d602af58a81a89228bc28f7e614bee3cb13f5bfb6430a0a30716"}, "provenance": "verbatim"}, "shard": "rust-csv", "status": "blocked", "subject": "csv-core: fix comment handling", "summary": "The NFA transition for the configured comment character was wired from `StartField`, so any field beginning with the comment byte \u2014 not just records starting with it \u2014 was treated as a comment (issue #137). Parsing `first,#tail\\n` under `comment = Some(b'#')` therefore dropped the second field. The fix moves the transition to `StartRecord`.", "updated_at": "2026-09-24T00:26:33.784990+00:00"}
